---
import ArticlePage from '@/components/articles/ArticlePage.astro';
import ArticleClosingNote from '@/components/articles/ArticleClosingNote.astro';
import ArticlePreviewCard from '@/components/ui/ArticlePreviewCard.astro';
import ArticleImage from '@/components/ui/ArticleImage.astro';
import { articleHref, articlesForDestination, getArticle } from '@/domains/articles/catalog';
import goldenHareExterior from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/golden-hare-books-exterior.webp';
import goldenHareInterior from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/golden-hare-books-interior.webp';
import toppingCompanyStorefront from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/topping-company-booksellers-storefront.webp';
import toppingCompanyInterior from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/topping-company-booksellers-interior.webp';
import armchairBooks from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/armchair-books-edinburgh.webp';
import tillsExterior from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/tills-bookshop-exterior.webp';
import tillsCorner from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/tills-bookshop-fireplace-corner.webp';
import bookLovers from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/book-lovers-bookshop.webp';
import lighthouseBookshop from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/lighthouse-bookshop-edinburgh.webp';
import typewrongerTypewriter from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/typewronger-books-typewriter.webp';
import typewrongerMap from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/typewronger-books-bookshop-map.webp';
import gentlyMadDownstairs from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/gently-mad-bookshop-downstairs.webp';
import gentlyMadOdyssey from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/gently-mad-bookshop-odyssey.webp';
import gentlyMadClassics from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/gently-mad-bookshop-classics.jpg';
import mcnaughtansEntrance from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/mcnaughtans-bookshop-entrance.webp';
import mcnaughtansInterior from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/mcnaughtans-bookshop-interior.webp';
import rareBirdsBooks from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/rare-birds-books.webp';
import waterstonesCafe from '@/assets/articles/edinburgh/waterstones-cafe-castle-view.webp';

const article = getArticle('best-bookshops-in-edinburgh')!;
const relatedArticles = articlesForDestination('scotland')
  .filter((a) => a.slug !== article.slug)
  .map((a) => ({
    href: articleHref(a.slug),
    image: a.image,
    category: a.category,
    title: a.title,
    alt: a.alt,
    comingSoon: a.comingSoon,
  }));
const sections = [
  { navTitle: 'Intro', target: 'section-intro' },
  { navTitle: '1. Golden Hare Books', target: 'bookshop-1' },
  { navTitle: '2. Topping & Company Booksellers', target: 'bookshop-2' },
  { navTitle: '3. Waterstones, Princes Street', target: 'bookshop-3' },
  { navTitle: '4. Rare Birds Books', target: 'bookshop-4' },
  { navTitle: '5. The Gently Mad Bookshop', target: 'bookshop-5' },
  { navTitle: '6. McNaughtan’s Bookshop', target: 'bookshop-6' },
  { navTitle: '7. Typewronger Books', target: 'bookshop-7' },
  { navTitle: '8. Armchair Books', target: 'bookshop-8' },
  { navTitle: '9. Book Lovers Bookshop', target: 'bookshop-9' },
  { navTitle: '10. Till’s Bookshop', target: 'bookshop-10' },
  { navTitle: '11. Lighthouse – Edinburgh’s Radical Bookshop', target: 'bookshop-11' },
  { navTitle: 'Final Thoughts', target: 'final-thoughts' },
] as const;
---

<ArticlePage article={article} sections={sections}>
  <figure slot="title-media">
    <ArticleImage
      src={article.lcpImage!}
      alt="Christmas decorations inside Waterstones Edinburgh"
      caption="Christmas decorations inside Waterstones Edinburgh"
      imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover"
      priority
    />
  </figure>

  <section id="bookshop-1" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">1. Golden Hare Books</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Golden Hare Books quickly became one of my favorites, thanks to its welcoming staff and cozy atmosphere. There’s even a real fireplace, which made the shop feel especially inviting when I visited in late autumn.</p>
      <p>The booksellers explained that the shop focuses mainly on new titles. If you can’t find what you’re looking for, you can check their online shop or ask them to order it for you. I couldn’t resist ordering a Christmas book during my visit, and it arrived just two days later!</p>
      <p>While you’re in Stockbridge, make time for a walk along Circus Lane, one of Edinburgh’s prettiest little streets, just a short walk from the bookshop.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage
          src={goldenHareExterior}
          alt="Exterior of Golden Hare Books in Stockbridge, Edinburgh"
          caption="Golden Hare Books in Stockbridge"
          imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
        />
        <ArticleImage
          src={goldenHareInterior}
          alt="Book-lined interior of Golden Hare Books"
          caption="Inside Golden Hare Books"
          imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-2" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">2. Topping &amp; Company Booksellers</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Topping &amp; Company was much larger than the independent bookshops I was used to visiting. Spread across two floors, it has separate rooms dedicated to different categories, with floor-to-ceiling shelves and rolling ladders that make you want to explore every corner.</p>
      <p>What struck me most was how bright the space felt despite all those towering bookshelves. Tall windows let in plenty of natural light, and the helpful staff make it easy to find your way around. If you have a little longer to spare, you can even enjoy a cup of tea or coffee while surrounded by books.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={toppingCompanyStorefront}
        alt="The curved storefront of Topping & Company Booksellers in Edinburgh"
        caption="Topping & Company Booksellers"
        imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover"
      />
      <ArticleImage
        src={toppingCompanyInterior}
        alt="The book-lined interior of Topping & Company Booksellers"
        caption="Inside Topping & Company Booksellers"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-3" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">3. Waterstones, Princes Street</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>I visited Waterstones in late October, just as the first Christmas decorations were appearing around the shop. As someone who loves Christmas, that was enough to put me in a good mood!</p>
      <p>The staff were friendly and happy to help, and, of course, I couldn’t leave empty-handed. I picked up a few things, including a beautiful jigsaw puzzle to take home. Thankfully, I was traveling with a very large suitcase!</p>
      <p>Even if you’re not planning to buy anything, head upstairs to Café W for a coffee with a view of Edinburgh Castle. The window seats are limited and tend to be popular, but there are plenty of other places to sit throughout the café.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={waterstonesCafe}
        alt="Waterstones cafe with Edinburgh Castle view"
        caption="Waterstones cafe with Edinburgh Castle view"
        imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-4" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">4. Rare Birds Books</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>With its pink decor and collection focused on women writers, Rare Birds Books has a clear identity of its own. I hadn’t come across a bookshop quite like it before, which made it an interesting stop during my wander around Edinburgh.</p>
      <p>If you’re looking to discover books by women writers, this is a place to spend some time. It’s also a reminder that bookshops don’t all have to follow the same formula; sometimes, a particular focus is what makes a shop stand out.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={rareBirdsBooks}
        alt="A beautiful collection of books by women"
        caption="A beautiful collection of books by women"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-5" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">5. The Gently Mad Bookshop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>The Gently Mad Bookshop is full of old, rare, and beautifully bound books that are hard for a book lover to resist. It’s a small shop, though, and when I visited on a Saturday around lunchtime, it was difficult to browse at my own pace.</p>
      <p>The shop has become popular on social media, which may have contributed to the crowds that day. I would have loved a little more room and time to look through the collection, so if you can, try visiting at a quieter hour.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={gentlyMadDownstairs}
        alt="The Gently Mad - A charming book-filled space tucked downstairs"
        caption="The Gently Mad - A charming book-filled space tucked downstairs"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage
          src={gentlyMadOdyssey}
          alt="The Gently Mad - A beautiful edition of a timeless classic"
          caption="The Gently Mad - A beautiful edition of a timeless classic"
          imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
        />
        <ArticleImage
          src={gentlyMadClassics}
          alt="The Gently Mad - Beautiful editions of beloved literary classics"
          caption="The Gently Mad - Beautiful editions of beloved literary classics"
          imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-6" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">6. McNaughtan’s Bookshop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>The moment you step inside McNaughtan’s Bookshop, you’re greeted by the unmistakable smell of old books. The wooden floor creaks beneath your feet, adding to the feeling that every corner holds a little piece of literary history.</p>
      <p>The shop specializes in second-hand books, and I noticed that prices were often penciled onto the first page. It’s a small detail, but one that suits the character of the place perfectly.</p>
      <p>If you enjoy the thrill of finding something unexpected among older titles, take your time here. You never know, you might just stumble upon a little treasure — and yes, I mean a book!</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={mcnaughtansEntrance}
        alt="McNaughtan’s - A bookshop tucked below street level"
        caption="McNaughtan’s - A bookshop tucked below street level"
        imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover"
      />
      <ArticleImage
        src={mcnaughtansInterior}
        alt="Old-world charm, wooden floors, and endless books"
        caption="Old-world charm, wooden floors, and endless books"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <div data-subscribe-after></div>

  <section id="bookshop-7" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">7. Typewronger Books</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Typewronger Books caught my attention with its vintage typewriters dotted around the shop alongside the books. They give the space a creative, slightly quirky feel, as though writing itself is part of the decor. It’s a fun place to stop if you appreciate the tools and traditions behind the written word, not just the finished books. The typewriters alone make it memorable. And if you buy a book, you can also pick up a free Edinburgh Bookshop Map to discover even more independent bookshops around the city.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={typewrongerTypewriter}
        alt="A creative corner for book and typewriter lovers"
        caption="A creative corner for book and typewriter lovers"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
      <ArticleImage
        src={typewrongerMap}
        alt="Pick up a free Edinburgh Bookshop Map with any book purchase"
        caption="Pick up a free Edinburgh Bookshop Map with any book purchase"
        imgClass="aspect-[4/5] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-8" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">8. Armchair Books</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Armchair Books is packed with second-hand books from floor to ceiling. The shelves are so full that there’s plenty to look through, whether you arrive with a particular title in mind or simply want to see what turns up.</p>
      <p>This is the kind of place where browsing is the main activity, so allow yourself a little time to look around rather than expecting a quick in-and-out visit.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={armchairBooks}
        alt="A charming second-hand bookshop in Edinburgh"
        caption="A charming second-hand bookshop in Edinburgh"
        imgClass="aspect-[5/4] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-9" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">9. Book Lovers Bookshop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Book Lovers Bookshop is a lovely find for anyone who enjoys romance novels, especially readers who appreciate special editions. Alongside the romantic fiction, you’ll find books with gorgeous covers and colorful sprayed edges — the decorative edges of the pages that make certain editions stand out on a bookshelf.</p>
      <p>If you enjoy collecting editions that look just as good as they read, you’ll want to take a closer look at the selection here.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={bookLovers}
        alt="A pretty pink haven for romance readers"
        caption="A pretty pink haven for romance readers"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-10" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">10. Till’s Bookshop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Till’s Bookshop is small and unassuming, with a wooden floor and a cozy corner featuring an old armchair beside a fireplace. When I visited, the fireplace wasn’t lit, but the little seating area still had an old-fashioned charm.</p>
      <p>There isn’t a huge amount to explore, so this probably won’t be the longest stop on your bookshop tour. Still, that quiet corner gives the shop a pleasant, lived-in feel.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-3 md:gap-4">
        <ArticleImage
          src={tillsExterior}
          alt="A lovely independent bookshop in Edinburgh"
          caption="A lovely independent bookshop in Edinburgh"
          imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
        />
        <ArticleImage
          src={tillsCorner}
          alt="A cozy little corner at Tills Bookshop"
          caption="A cozy little corner at Tills Bookshop"
          imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="bookshop-11" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="mb-5 max-w-3xl text-black md:mb-6">
      <h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-semibold text-neutral-900 mb-4">11. Lighthouse – Edinburgh’s Radical Bookshop</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80 [&_p]:mb-5 [&_p:last-child]:mb-0">
      <p>Lighthouse has a more alternative feel than a conventional bookshop, with a focus on radical ideas, politics, and social change. Its collection offers a different perspective from the fiction and second-hand titles you’ll find elsewhere on this list.</p>
      <p>It’s particularly worth a look if you’re interested in social and political issues or want to explore books that question established ideas. Even if that isn’t your usual reading territory, it adds another dimension to Edinburgh’s bookshop scene.</p>
      <ArticleImage
        src={lighthouseBookshop}
        alt="Discovering the more unusual corners of Lighthouse"
        caption="Discovering the more unusual corners of Lighthouse"
        imgClass="aspect-[2/3] object-cover"
      />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="final-thoughts" class="scroll-mt-nav">
    <div class="article-prose max-w-3xl text-black/80">
      <ArticleClosingNote label="Final thoughts">
        <p>Golden Hare Books and Waterstones were my personal favorites, each for different reasons. Golden Hare won me over with its welcoming atmosphere and real fireplace, while Waterstones gave me the chance to browse for a few treats beyond books. I even brought home a beautiful jigsaw puzzle!</p>
        <p>Topping &amp; Company would be a close third. Its impressive scale, tall shelves, and large windows made it particularly memorable. Between the three, I found very different reasons to linger — whether it was the warmth of a small independent shop, the view of the castle, or simply being surrounded by books and having time to look around.</p>
      </ArticleClosingNote>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section slot="before-footer" class="mx-auto w-full max-w-6xl px-4 md:pr-10 md:pl-0 pb-16 md:pb-20">
    <h2 class="mb-8 md:mb-10">You may also like</h2>
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 sm:grid-cols-2 sm:gap-10 lg:grid-cols-3">
      {relatedArticles.map((related) => (
        <ArticlePreviewCard {...related} />
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
</ArticlePage>
